<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n37212" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">post-hăbĕo</span></b> ,
			ŭi, ĭtum, 2, v. a.,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>to place
			after</i>, <i>esteem less</i>, <i>postpone</i>, <i>neglect</i> (class.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">omnes posthabui mihi res,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ter.
					Phorm. 5, 7, 15</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">omnia,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Caes.
					B. C. 3, 33</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">omnibus rebus posthabitis,</span>”
				<i>neglecting every thing</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Tusc. 5, 1, 2</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">posthabitā Samo,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Verg.
					A. 1, 16</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">posthabitam dote solatus est,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Tac. A.
					2, 86</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">id.
				H. 4, 7</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">posthabui illorum mea seria ludo,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Verg.
					E. 7, 17</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
